# shadcn Components Only

All UI primitives and interactive controls must come from shadcn/ui in this project. Do not introduce other component libraries or one-off custom primitives when a shadcn equivalent exists or can be added.

## Requirements

- Use components from `web/src/components/ui/` (Button, Input, Dialog, Sheet, Select, Tabs, Card, Table, etc.).
- If a needed shadcn component is missing, add it via the project’s shadcn CLI (`npx shadcn@latest add …`) — do not hand-roll a parallel primitive.
- Compose pages from shadcn primitives + layout markup. Domain components (e.g. `NotificationBell`) may wrap shadcn, but the underlying controls stay shadcn.
- Prefer built-in variants (`variant`, `size`) and semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) over custom colors or one-off styled elements.
- Do **not** add MUI, Chakra, Ant Design, Headless UI (standalone), React Bootstrap, or similar unless the user explicitly asks.

## Exceptions

- Allowed only when the user specifically requests a non-shadcn library or custom control.
- Icons: continue using the project’s existing icon approach (e.g. `lucide-react`) — icons are not a competing component library.
- App-level routing, data, and domain logic are out of scope for this rule.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-4 py-2 text-white">Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
<Button>Save</Button>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom modal when Dialog/Sheet exists
<div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 ...">...</div>

// ✅ GOOD
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle } from "@/components/ui/dialog"
```
